  "response": "**Solution**\n\nLet A = multiples of 3 or 5 (from 1–1000), and we need to exclude those also divisible by 7.\n\n**Step 1: Count multiples of 3 or 5**\n- ⌊1000/3⌋ = 333\n- ⌊1000/5⌋ = 200\n- ⌊1000/15⌋ = 66\n- |A| = 333 + 200 − 66 = 467\n\n**Step 2: Count multiples of 3 or 5 that are also divisible by 7** (i.e., divisible by 21 or 35)\n- ⌊1000/21⌋ = 47\n- ⌊1000/35⌋ = 28\n- ⌊1000/105⌋ = 9 (lcm(21,35)=105)\n- Count = 47 + 28 − 9 = 66\n\n**Step 3: Subtract**\n467 − 66 = 401\n\nFINAL ANSWER: 401",
